### 🚀 **Performance Profiling**

To ensure efficiency, especially for large-scale multi-body simulations, we'll prepare the code for profiling.

```cpp
// Example: A performance benchmark to simulate gravitational calculations over many objects
void benchmarkGravityCalculations(int numBodies) {
    std::vector<std::pair<double, double>> bodies(numBodies);
    std::vector<double> masses(numBodies);

    // Initialize dummy values
    for (int i = 0; i < numBodies; ++i) {
        bodies[i] = {1.0, 1.0};
        masses[i] = 1.0;
    }

    // Perform a batch calculation
    auto start = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();

    for (int i = 0; i < numBodies; ++i) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < numBodies; ++j) {
            calculateGravitationalForce(masses[i], masses[j], 1e9);
        }
    }

    auto end = std::chrono::high_resolution_clock::now();
    std::chrono::duration<double> elapsed = end - start;

    std::cout << "Benchmark completed in " << elapsed.count() << " seconds" << std::endl;
}
```

